# Story 84: Humanoids vs Agents (40s)
# Hook: Same brain, same skill format -- agents face inward, humanoids face the world.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-084-humanoids-vs-agents.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Same brain, same skill format -- agents face inward, humanoids face the world.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Launch rysh and drop into rysh mode. Let's spawn one of each and compare them side by side.

[00:09.0 --> 00:17.0]
An agent is an internal worker -- no terminal, no external reach. Perfect for reviewing code or running tasks inside the workspace.

[00:17.0 --> 00:25.0]
A humanoid is the same agent plus external channels. Same skill file format -- it just adds a contacts block.

[00:25.0 --> 00:34.0]
And the at-sign and double-at-sign prefixes work for both -- Rysh resolves the name across both registries automatically.

[00:34.0 --> 00:40.0]
Agents are your internal team; humanoids are your public face. One format, two reaches.

